
# The Term site-asset accessor, the `@term/site` port of the React the React site-asset accessor. It
# resolves a logical asset path (`/CrowMark.otf`, `/logo.png`) to its current content-hashed immutable URL on
# `site.clue.surf` -- the SAME host + `cluesurfsite` R2 bucket the React sites use, so a Term site's fonts / logos /
# images resolve to the same hashed CDN objects. Pages / components consume it: `load @term/site/code/base/asset/asset`
# then `call get-site-asset-path` with a logical path, and `bind src` / `bind href` the result.
#
# The manifest itself lives in the native runtime shim (./runtime/asset.ts), a self-contained snapshot regenerated by
# the sync task. This module docks that shim as <global:asset> and exposes the public accessor surface as `.tree`
# tasks, exactly mirroring asset.ts's functions: `get-site-asset-path` (throws on unknown, so misspelled paths fail at
# the call site), `try-get-site-asset-path` (null on missing), `get-site-asset-entry` (the full entry or null), plus
# `site-assets` (the bare table) and `site-assets-manifest` (the whole manifest).
#
# Spec: note/platform/infrastructure/site-asset-sync.md

dock load
  load <global:asset>, name asset
  note native

# Resolve a logical asset path to its current hashed URL on site.clue.surf. Throws if the asset is not in the
# manifest (matching getSiteAssetPath), so a misspelled path fails loudly instead of producing a broken URL.
task get-site-asset-path
  take logical-path, like text
  like text
  send back
    call asset/get
      read logical-path

# Resolve safely -- returns null if the asset is missing rather than throwing. For optional assets where a missing
# entry shouldn't crash the page (matching tryGetSiteAssetPath).
task try-get-site-asset-path
  take logical-path, like text
  send back
    call asset/try-get
      read logical-path

# The full entry (link + code + hash + size) for diagnostics / debug surfaces, or null if missing (matching
# getSiteAssetEntry).
task get-site-asset-entry
  take logical-path, like text
  send back
    call asset/entry
      read logical-path

# The bare `assets` table, for direct iteration (matching the SITE_ASSETS export).
task site-assets
  send back
    call asset/all

# The full manifest, for advanced callers (matching the SITE_ASSETS_MANIFEST export).
task site-assets-manifest
  send back
    call asset/manifest
